 "transcript": [
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "bosch washer FD 9409 not draining. ive cleaned the filter already. what part do i need?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "I can't recommend a specific part yet because \"not draining\" after cleaning the filter usually points to a blockage or a pump issue rather than a single failed component. The most common next cause is something stuck in the pump impeller or a kinked drain hose, so we need to check that first. Please switch off and unplug the machine, then shine a torch into the filter hole and gently turn the small plastic fan blades inside with your finger. Let me know if they spin freely or if you feel anything caught or jammed in them."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "ok did that, it turns but feels a bit stiff and gritty in places. also E18 came up on the display last time it stalled"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "That gritty feeling suggests there may be debris still caught in the pump impeller preventing it from spinning freely. Before we consider replacing any parts, please try to gently dislodge anything stuck behind those fan blades with a non-metallic tool like a plastic knife or tweezers. Once you've done that, let me know if the blades spin more smoothly and whether the machine starts draining now."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "I'm not taking the machine apart beyond the filter, I haven't got the tools for the sump. Is there any other check I can do, or is it the pump? Which part do I order?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "AI service unavailable. Please try again in a moment."
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Your last reply just said 'AI service unavailable', so nothing came through. Can you resend? Is it the pump, and which part do I order?"
  },
  {
   "role": "assistant",
   "text": "[Heading: Likely cause: drain pump]\nThe checks you've done point to the drain pump being faulty due to that gritty resistance, but I cannot confirm which specific part number fits your Bosch FD 9409 model. Since the impeller is stiff and you are not comfortable opening the machine further, it is best not to guess at a replacement part or attempt a repair without the correct tools. The most reliable next step is to contact Bosch's official manufacturer spares service or book an engineer who can identify the exact component for your specific model."
  }
 ],
